{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1135520-advice-on-a-fiction-idea","id":1135520,"title":"Advice on a fiction idea","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-30T11:39:07-07:00","id":1135520,"title":"Advice on a fiction idea","content":"I was watching some Tales From the Crypt recently and it reminded me of a piece of fiction i saw in the preview from the Bone Gnawers 1st ed tribebook. That's when i thought up this idea. How about having three Tales from the Crypt-like stories set in the CWoD? The basic idea is to make three short stories, set in Vampire, Werewolf and Mage. Like in Tales, the main characters in these stories are people who get their just desserts in the end of the stories. In Vampire, the main character is a unscrupulous travel agent. In Werewolf, it is a predatory loan shark and in Mage, it is a crooked stock broker. In all three of these stories, the character get ironic punishments that would fit in the gameline it is set in.<br /> <br /> I want advice on what these ironic punishments should be. Also, i would like help coming up with a Crypt Keeper-style host to guide you through these stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T12:50:16-07:00","id":1135554,"title":"","content":"I don't know for the vampire, but the werewolf could get hunted by a Hunter, maybe a big game hunter type. The mage seems like either a Syndicate member or maybe a member of the Order of Hermes. He could ultimatly be hunted down by the opposite faction and end up a beggar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:21:22-07:00","id":1135568,"title":"","content":"Are the characters supernatural or human?<br /> <br /> Usually Tales of the Crypt characters are human. It could be an interesting play, having the monsters actually <i>being </i>the monsters.for a change","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T13:37:31-07:00","id":1135577,"title":"","content":"They are human. For the loan shark story, I think making the monster a Werewolf is to predictable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-30T18:10:36-07:00","id":1135645,"title":"","content":"Here is the synopsis for the Vampire story<br /> <br /> &quot; Meet Henry Carlston, a real estate that specializes in selling people timeshares. For years, Henry and his accomplice, Barney, have been selling phony time shares to the gullible, especially elderly people. Recently, Henry and Barney arrived in Romania shortly after the collapse of it's communist government to buy land from gullible farmers who sell their land for almost 75% less than it's worth. One night, the two get caught in a storm in take shelter in the home of a eccentric old man. But, unknown to them, the old man has a dark secret that both Henry and Barney will soon discover&quot;.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think so far?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-01T15:15:52-07:00","id":1136393,"title":"","content":"Here is the Werewolf synopsis.<br /> &quot; Arnold De la Chance is a one of New York City's most infamous loan shark. He has the reputation of ruthlessly hunting anyone who owes him money, giving him the reputation of being a predator. He is currently trying to find Edwardo Sanchez, a man who who him $200,000.00. However, the predator is about to become the prey when Edwardo is transformed into a fomori.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12186-killerclown","name":"Killerclown","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"819"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}